      "worked_solution": "We are given that the part is $36,$ the percentage is $50\\%,$ and we need to find the whole.\n\nTo do this, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{whole} = \\textrm{part} \\div \\textrm{percentage}\n$$\n\nBefore we can substitute our numbers into the formula, we need to express $50\\%$ as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{50}{100} = \\dfrac{50\\div 50}{100\\div 50} = \\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nWe can now substitute our numbers into the formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{whole} & =36÷50% \\\\  & =36÷\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =36\\times \\frac{2}{1} \\\\  & =36\\times 2 \\\\  & =72\\end{aligned}\n$$",
